{"id":"translator-and-historical-edition-notes-part-9","label":"Translator and historical edition notes (part 9)","headingNoteRefs":"","context":"","kind":"commentary","blocks":[{"text":"[^n3358]: Matt. xxvi. 50c.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3358"},{"text":"[^n3359]: Luke xxii. 49.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3359"},{"text":"[^n3360]: John xviii. 10.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3360"},{"text":"[^n3361]: John xviii. 11a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3361"},{"text":"[^n3362]: John xviii. 11c; Matt. xxvi. 52b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3362"},{"text":"[^n3363]: Withis doubtless an accidental repetition of by (the same Arabic particle) in the next clause.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3363"},{"text":"[^n3364]: Matt. xxvi. 53.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3364"},{"text":"[^n3365]: The introductory interrogative particle may represent an original Or.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3365"},{"text":"[^n3366]: Vat. ms. omits than, and has more only in the margin by another hand.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3366"},{"text":"[^n3367]: Matt. xxvi. 54.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3367"},{"text":"[^n3368]: Luke xxii. 51b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3368"},{"text":"[^n3369]: The phrase is awkward. The rendering is different in the text (f. 292a, cf. Lagarde, Die vier Evv.), and yet again in the comment (f. 293a) of Ibn-at-Tayyib’s Commentary.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3369"},{"text":"[^n3370]: Matt. xxvi. 55.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3370"},{"text":"[^n3371]: Luke xxii. 53b.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3371"},{"text":"[^n3372]: Matt. xxvi. 56.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3372"},{"text":"[^n3373]: John xviii. 12a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3373"},{"text":"[^n3374]: cf. § 11, 11.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3374"},{"text":"[^n3375]: Mark xiv. 51.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3375"},{"text":"[^n3376]: Lit. one.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3376"},{"text":"[^n3377]: Mark xiv. 52.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"