"},{"text":"[^n3586]: The Arabic text has deriding (cf. § 51, 37). Either with is accidentally omitted, or, more probably, we should correct the spelling to shaking (cf. Syriac versions).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3586"},{"text":"[^n3587]: Matt. xxvii. 40a; Mark xv. 29.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3587"},{"text":"[^n3588]: Matt. xxvii. 40c.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3588"},{"text":"[^n3589]: Matt. xxvii. 41.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3589"},{"text":"[^n3590]: Matt. xxvii. 42a.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3590"},{"text":"[^n3591]: Luke xxiii. 35c; Matt. xxvii. 42c.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3591"},{"text":"[^n3592]: Verse 37 or Mt.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3592"},{"text":"[^n3593]: Matt. xxvii. 43.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3593"},{"text":"[^n3594]: Luke xxiii. 36.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3594"},{"text":"[^n3595]: Luke xxiii. 37.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3595"},{"text":"[^n3596]: Matt. xxvii. 44.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3596"},{"text":"[^n3597]: Borg. ms. has boys (an easy clerical error).","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3597"},{"text":"[^n3598]: Luke xxiii. 39.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3598"},{"text":"[^n3599]: Luke xxiii. 40.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3599"},{"text":"[^n3600]: Luke xxiii. 41.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3600"},{"text":"[^n3601]: Our deed might be read we have done, and perhaps our translator’s style would justify our writing as for to.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3601"},{"text":"[^n3602]: Luke xxiii. 42.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3602"},{"text":"[^n3603]: Luke xxiii. 43.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3603"},{"text":"[^n3604]: Borg. ms. has Verily, verily.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3604"},{"text":"[^n3605]: John xix. 25.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3605"},{"text":"[^n3606]: A single word in Arabic.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3606"},{"text":"[^n3607]: Vat. ms. has and Mary.","kind":"commentary","noteId":"n3607"},{"text":"[^n3608]: John xix.